// Real case: Jerome et al., Nature Communications 2020 / Aubert et al., Nature Communications 2024
//
// HSV-2 latent reservoir excision using dual meganuclease / CRISPR guides
// targeting the HSV-2 genome in latently infected sacral dorsal root ganglia.
//
// Published outcome (Aubert et al. 2024, doi:10.1038/s41467-024-45030-1):
//   - AAV-delivered meganucleases targeting HSV in mouse DRG
//   - ~90-97% reduction in latent HSV DNA in sacral ganglia
//   - Complete elimination NOT achieved
//   - Some animals showed undetectable viral DNA, most did not
//
// Known ground truth: eliminates_reservoir should be REFUSED.
// The therapy reduces but does not eliminate the latent reservoir.
// Key gaps: outcome distribution unmeasured in humans, residence
// not proven exhaustive (HSV latency may extend beyond sacral DRG).

target HSV2Latent {
  organism human
  tolerance 0
  signatures all [ GATCTTGGACGT, TTACGCAAGCTT ]
  in [ neuron.sensory.sacral ] @asserted(human)
}

excise HSV2Latent
